  "format": 1,
  "about": "Scenarios of one node of the multinode extension, with the expectations written by hand from docs/MULTINODE.md. Hex strings have no separators; ids are written 0xNNN; 't' is the offset in ms from the start of the node, whose clock is the 32-bit millisecond counter of the board. 'verdict' is what the node does with the received frame: 'pass' hands it to the single-head dispatcher, 'consume' keeps it. 'emit' lists, in order, the frames the node has due after that frame; 'may' is whether it may obey single-head frames at that moment.",
